<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 2: </span><span id="A0.T2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Effect of Feature Selection on Proxy Learning Performance.</span> Including both contrastive and independent scores alongside sparsity achieves the highest Correct Ranking Pair Ratio (CRPR) of 75.98%. Removing either score leads to a slight drop, while adding a joint score does not improve performance. Excluding sparsity significantly reduces accuracy, confirming its importance in interpretability prediction.</figcaption>
